englishSenses.definition:
a. Signifying many different things; of manifold meaning;
   equivocal.
n. A multivocal word.

n. The state or quality of being reluctant; repugnance;
   aversion of mind; unwillingness; -- often followed by an infinitive, or
   by to and a noun, formerly sometimes by against.

n. A scale series of four sounds, of which the extremes,
   or first and last, constituted a fourth. These extremes were immutable;
   the two middle sounds were changeable.
